  "content": "In mid-May, a group known as La Pampa Leaks claimed to have compromised Uruguay's government-sponsored identity service managed by telecommunications provider Antel, reportedly monetizing the information as a citizen-data lookup service. In February, a hacking collective known as the Chronus Group claimed to have stolen data from 25 different Mexican government agencies and groups . And, in Colombia, cyberattackers targeted the nation's health ministry with more than 23 million attempted attacks during the month of March.",
